# --- task-specific work products: personal/company data, never for the public repo
# (folder READMEs and the example skill are kept as reference)
# Brain/ is the AI knowledge base: company-confidential product specs and
# ~1,300 fetched Confluence pages. This repo has a PUBLIC remote, so this rule
# is the only thing keeping that content off GitHub. Do not relax it, and do
# not 'git add -f' anything beneath it.
Brain/
Output/*
!Output/README.md
!Output/worklog/
Output/worklog/*
!Output/worklog/README.md
# Renamed from Skill/ — and the rename silently voided the old rules, because
# git matches these case-sensitively even on a case-insensitive filesystem. All
# eleven workplace skills were staged again as a result, having been excluded
# since the repo went public. Rename this folder and you must rename these lines
# in the same commit; the allowlist below is the only thing keeping them local.
skills/*
!skills/README.md
!skills/_example/
!skills/worklog/
# automation/ is allowlisted: anything dropped in here is local until it is
# explicitly un-ignored, so workplace-specific jobs can never be staged by accident
automation/*
!automation/cindex-refresh.sh
!automation/launchd/
# ...but the local agent manifest is workplace-specific by design
automation/launchd/agents.local.json
ENHANCEMENTS.md

# --- usage data & logs
*.log
logs/
automation/*.log

# --- secrets & local config (values belong in claude-vault, not files)
.env
*.env

# --- build/interpreter artefacts
# no trailing-slash-only anchor: these must match at any depth, not just the root
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- OS/editor noise
.DS_Store
*.tmp
*.zip
*.bak
